From: Bonito Port Team <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] opengl: skip swapchain fences for external FBO contexts

libmpv's OpenGL render API passes an empty ra_ctx_params because its caller
owns presentation. Without a swap_buffers callback, the fence queue can never
be drained. Backport the current mpv behavior and avoid creating the latency
simulation fences for that external swapchain.

diff --git a/video/out/opengl/context.c b/video/out/opengl/context.c
--- a/video/out/opengl/context.c
+++ b/video/out/opengl/context.c
@@ -232,7 +232,7 @@ bool ra_gl_ctx_submit_frame(struct ra_swapchain *sw, const struct vo_frame *fram
     if (p->opts->use_glfinish)
         gl->Finish();
 
-    if (gl->FenceSync) {
+    if (gl->FenceSync && p->params.swap_buffers) {
         GLsync fence = gl->FenceSync(GL_SYNC_GPU_COMMANDS_COMPLETE, 0);
         if (fence)
             MP_TARRAY_APPEND(p, p->vsync_fences, p->num_vsync_fences, fence);
